{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>יִחְפְּשׂוּ</b> — from the binyan qal, and the future tense is opened [with a yod] because of the guttural letter, like יָעִלְצוּ חֲסִידִים בְכָבוֹד." "<b>עֻלּוֹת</b> — from the root עול, like וַעֲלָתָהּ קָפְצָה פִיהָ. And the view of the grammarians of Sepharad: כִּי חַסְדֵי יְהוָה כִּי לֹא תָמְנוּ is like תַּמּוּ, and the nun is in place of the letter of doubling, and the proof for this is כִּי לֹא כָלוּ רַחֲמָיו. And the proof, second: that we do not find from this root in verbs with missing ayin — which the sages of France call weak — a pattern like [the proposed reading]. And the proof, third: that תָּמְנוּ — searched in the searched-out text — is absent from the etnaḥ; it is pašta. And had it been like כִּי עַתָּה שָׁבְנוּ it would be with qamatz. And behold, its accent is שֶׁיִּתְמּוּ. Searched in the searched-out text, and all this in secret, and this is the meaning of וְקָרַב אִישׁ וְלֵב עָמֹק."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 64, :notes {1 "The text is highly compressed and cryptic throughout; several clauses are elliptical and the second proof appears to contain a lacuna or corruption. Rendered hyper-literally. The accent name שיתמו in the third proof is obscure, possibly a ta'am name or a textual corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:48.007469694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}